{
  "additional_concerns": [
    "The advertising duties and attribution risk are supported but do not determine gift classification. Their absence from these gift-only formulas is not an omission of an applicable condition, and these labels do not authorize deleting the claims.",
    "Candidates node.2a6321b4ce90763bf0be564e, node.6d6e7adc6faa9d94b74c08e5, node.968dbccb08282a4e8a580ae5, node.97af37a2579f59b0ee43211f and node.bca408c75cbf8467afafada6 place offering or promotional conditions in Scope. Their executable semantics return OUT_OF_SCOPE when those conditions are false, rather than the question's stated negative prohibition result or positive gift-control compliance result. Whether this is intended requires an explicit question-domain restriction.",
    "The offer-level candidates combine an offer-level promotional connection with existence of a non-discount gift component. In a mixed offer, this may catch a component without establishing that the component itself has the required promotional connection. Establish whether the connection necessarily applies to every assessed component or retain it inside the existential component test.",
    "A TRUE_IS_COMPLIANT result for node.6d6e7adc6faa9d94b74c08e5 addresses only the selected gift control. It does not establish compliance with advertising duties, section 103, or other requirements.",
    "The circular expressly defines distributors by reference to SFC-authorised funds. Broader distributor and product wording in some candidates needs to retain that source scope unless a broader paragraph 3.11 assessment is separately intended and supported.",
    "The source supports offering as the relevant act and does not require receipt or payment. However, node.bc55be7e973a689d07f9e64b's categorical statements about funding and fulfilment independence are not expressly resolved by the supplied text; attribution remains a factual and interpretive question.",
    "No external dependencies are supplied. Independent verification of the broader legal standards would require the applicable Code of Conduct paragraphs 3.11 and 2.3, the answer to question 1 of the SFC FAQ issued on 30 September 2010, and the Advertising Guidelines with applicable supplements. The Handbook provision identified in footnote 1 would be needed to verify the underlying disclosure duty. These missing texts do not prevent support assessments of the circular's express statements.",
    "The supplied text contains no operative date interval for these controls. The representations' temporal uncertainty semantics do not independently establish which legal version applies."
  ],
